FILE	AGENTS.md
# Kira Desktop contributor and agent rules

## Visual stack (mandatory)

- **Apache ECharts** is the project's charting library for all new or redesigned
  charts, gauges, trends and quantitative visualizations. Do not hand-draw charts
  with ad-hoc CSS bars, SVG paths or an additional charting library.
  Prefer tree-shakable `echarts/core` imports, register only required modules
  and choose SVG rendering for compact WebKitGTK overlays.
- **GSAP** is the project's JavaScript animation library. Use it for deliberate
  motion such as entry transitions, numeric emphasis and state changes rather
  than introducing a second JS animation framework or complex CSS keyframes.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` everywhere, and retain accessible labels,
  meaningful numeric fallback text, keyboard focus and functional no-motion UI.
  Never animate fake data into a chart or replace missing sensor data with zero.
- **Lifecycle matters:** WebKit widgets mount only while requested. Instantiate
  ECharts and GSAP effects on mount, resize charts when geometry changes,
  dispose chart instances, kill GSAP tweens and detach observers on unmount.
  Never create unmanaged timers, background data polling or repeated listeners.
- **Offline WebKit constraint:** The packaged frontend is a single
  self-contained HTML document. All npm code is bundled locally, with no CDN,
  runtime fetches, unexpected JS chunks or external stylesheets. Keep
  `frontend/scripts/inline-assets.mjs` and its tests passing.
- Retain the canonical five-color Kira palette in
  `frontend/src/lib/themes/kira-default.css`, the 42px top bar, and the
  locked-down Rust/GIO ↔ WebKit bridge. Charts are read-only presentation.

## Build and review

Changes to runtime JS dependencies require updates to both
`frontend/package.json` and `frontend/package-lock.json`, plus the
frontend Nix dependency hash in `nix/package.nix`. Run `task check`,
`task frontend:build` and (for frontend lock updates) `nix build .#frontend`.
Test supported and unavailable metrics, bounded history, reduced motion,
and open/close cleanup. Visual-QA check the popup in isolated nested Niri.

FILE	Cargo.toml
[workspace]
resolver = "2"
members = [
  "crates/kira-ipc",
  "crates/kira-core",
  "crates/kira-shell",
]

[workspace.package]
edition = "2024"
version = "0.1.0"
license = "MIT"

[workspace.dependencies]
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }

# Debug symbols are expensive for GTK/WebKit bindings and not required for
# routine visual preview. Incremental compilation stays enabled by default.
[profile.dev]
debug = 0

FILE	README.md
# Kira Desktop

**Status:** v0.1 Draft, working foundation, **not yet an MVP desktop environment**.

Kira Desktop is a modular, declarative, NixOS-first shell for Niri/Wayland. Rust owns system capabilities, Svelte 5 owns the UI and KDL will define layouts.

- [Technical specification (Russian)](docs/SPECIFICATION.md)
- [Development guide](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md)
- [Kira Default design system](docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md)
- [CI checks](.github/workflows/ci.yml)
- [Native Nix build checks](.github/workflows/nix.yml)
- [Visual QA / packaged Shell smoke-test guide](docs/QA_VISUAL.md)

## Implemented foundation

| Component | Current capabilities |
| --- | --- |
| `crates/kira-ipc` | JSON-RPC 2.0 contracts, bounded Unix socket client, unit tests |
| `crates/kira-core` | Tokio daemon exposing `ping` and `get_state` over a configurable user-owned Unix socket |
| `crates/kira-shell` | GTK4/WebKitGTK 6 layer-shell host with a WebKit-to-Rust-to-Core bridge and a native Gio application Launcher |
| `frontend/` | Svelte 5, Tailwind CSS v4 via Vite, typed Kira Default design tokens, editorial top bar, native Launcher trigger, Core status and workspace SDK, Vitest |
| `Taskfile.yml` | Shared commands for development and CI |
| `flake.nix`, `nix/package.nix` | Nix development shell and installable packaged Core/Shell/frontend |
| `Cargo.lock`, `flake.lock`, `frontend/package-lock.json` | Locked dependencies for reproducibility |

## Safe nested preview on NixOS

The recommended development entry point runs a **separate, windowed Niri** with
its own Kira Core socket and isolated Niri config, without replacing your current
desktop session:

```sh
nix develop --command task dev:preview
```

The default preview uses `cargo build --locked` and a local Vite build. Cargo
reuses `target/debug` between runs, avoiding a full Nix release rebuild after
each Rust or Svelte edit. On first run, WebKitGTK Rust bindings must still
compile. For the packaged release build instead, use:

```sh
nix develop --command task dev:preview:release
```

To reopen a previously built development preview with **no build step**,
use `task dev:preview:run` inside `nix develop`.

Close the window with **Alt+Shift+Q** (inside nested Niri) or press **Ctrl+C** in
the launching terminal. This only stops preview-owned processes. No `nixos-rebuild
switch`, global `pkill`, systemd manipulation or modification of
`~/.config/niri` is involved.

See [safe preview guide (Russian)](docs/PREVIEW.md). The preview lifecycle is
tested with mock Niri/Core/Shell processes in CI, but the first visual smoke test
on your GPU and Niri session must still be performed locally.

## Quick start on NixOS

Ensure Niri and a working Wayland session are available, then:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/iivkis/kira-desktop.git
cd kira-desktop
nix build
```

Run these in **separate terminals** inside the Niri session:

```sh
./result/bin/kira-core
```

```sh
./result/bin/kira-shell
```

For development and tests:

```sh
nix develop
npm ci --prefix frontend
task check
task shell:check
task build
```

Nix CI on Linux has successfully compiled the native Shell, built the package and run the Rust tests. **The top bar was manually rendered successfully inside a nested Niri window**; a full desktop session and packaged-system installation still require additional testing.

## Compact source context for agents (RepoSpool)

[`.repospool`](.repospool) is a **generated**, deterministic
`REPOSPOOL/1.0` snapshot of committed UTF-8 sources. It provides a compact
file/line index, the original selected file bytes, and the pinned source
commit. It does not guess code semantics or replace GitHub source links.

[`.repospoolignore`](.repospoolignore) keeps the snapshot focused on Core,
IPC, Shell, Svelte, Nix, tests, CI and the design specification. Dependency
lockfiles, local build/cache outputs, the bootstrap lockfile workflow and
historical preview troubleshooting are omitted **only from the snapshot**,
not from the repository. Missing context can still be read directly from GitHub.

On each `main` source commit,
[`Publish RepoSpool context`](.github/workflows/publish-repospool.yml)
regenerates and verifies the snapshot using a pinned upstream RepoSpool
revision, then publishes it in a separate artifact-only commit. Accordingly,
the `C` source revision inside `.repospool` can differ from the current
`main` HEAD by that publication commit. Verify origin and revision before
using it to make repository changes.

To generate or verify locally with the upstream CLI:

```sh
nix run github:iivkis/repospool -- generate .
nix run github:iivkis/repospool -- verify --artifact .repospool --repo .
```


## Pull request checks

The CI workflow reports two stable jobs on pull requests: **Core + Svelte checks**
and **Native Shell check**. The second job invokes
`nix develop .#ci --command cargo check --locked -p kira-shell --all-targets`
when Rust Shell/IPC code, Cargo/Nix dependencies, or the CI configuration changes.
Unrelated UI/docs-only PRs skip the native dependency setup without leaving a
missing check status. The slim `.#ci` dev shell excludes the compositor and
visual-preview tools; Nix binary inputs come from its configured caches, and
GitHub Actions caches the Rust dependencies. The full Nix release package remains
on its separate nightly/manual workflow.

To **enforce** the native job on protected branches, require the status check
`Native Shell check` in the repository's branch protection/ruleset, alongside
`Core + Svelte checks`.

## IPC subscription liveness

Core pushes workspace and validated KDL config updates immediately when they change.
If nothing changes, it sends a read-only JSON-RPC heartbeat every **5 seconds**
on each subscription using the same request id and the distinct
`{"heartbeat":true}` result. Heartbeats do **not** repeat workspace/config
snapshots or generate browser events. Shell's blocking IPC workers use a
**15-second socket read timeout**: a connected but unresponsive Core causes
the existing reconnect loop to run, mark workspaces offline, and retry. The
last valid config is retained while reconnecting. The heartbeat is internal
to the Core/Shell protocol, not part of the WebKit JS allowlist.

## Incremental and release build caching

- **Local Rust development:** `nix develop` sets up persistent `sccache`
  (and Cargo still reuses `target/debug`), so recompilation can reuse compiler
  outputs between development runs.
- **Reproducible release:** `nix build .#default` uses Crane to cache compiled
  third-party Rust crates separately from application code and separately from
  the frontend. Changing Svelte should not rebuild Rust; changing a Rust
  source file should not rebuild GTK/WebKit Rust crates.
- **Fresh CI machines:** an optional shared Cachix binary cache can be enabled
  through repository settings. Without it, cached artifacts persist only
  locally in each machine's Nix store. See
  [build cache guide](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md#build-caching-and-release-iteration).

A new dependency-cache derivation must be compiled once on the first build;
changing `Cargo.lock`, manifests, toolchain, native libraries or relevant
Nix inputs may legitimately invalidate the cache.

## Default theme: Black, Prussian Blue and Orange

The built-in **Kira Default** dark theme uses five fully opaque colors:

`#000000ff` Black · `#14213dff` Prussian Blue · `#fca311ff` Orange ·
`#e5e5e5ff` Alabaster Grey · `#ffffffff` White.

These colors drive the Svelte Top Bar, pre-mount WebKit loading screen and
native GTK Launcher. Black is the background, Prussian Blue makes structured
surfaces, Orange marks focus and selection, Alabaster Grey is secondary text,
and White is primary text. Selected Orange surfaces use **Black** text for
contrast. Semantic tokens derive from the five canonical palette values;
custom KDL theme overrides remain a future feature. See the
[design system](docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md) for exact mappings and WCAG checks.

## Validated KDL settings (Stage 2 draft)

Kira Core can read `~/.config/kira-desktop/config.kdl` (or an absolute
`KIRA_CONFIG_FILE` override), validate a **small, documented KDL profile**
and hot-reload UI settings without restarting the compositor, Core or Shell.
Settings include compact Top Bar spacing, center title, clock seconds,
workspace names and maximum visible workspace chips. If an edit is invalid,
the previous valid config stays active and the Top Bar shows `CONFIG !`.

Copy the [sample configuration](config/kira.kdl.example), validate a file
with `kira-core --check-config /absolute/path/config.kdl`, and read the
[supported KDL syntax and safe preview guide](docs/CONFIG.md).

The current KDL profile deliberately **does not implement full KDL grammar**,
arbitrary commands, Niri actions or external modules. The independent Niri
preview generates a temporary editable Kira config for experimentation.

## Real Niri workspaces (Stage 1 draft)

The Top Bar obtains **real Niri workspace state** through
`NIRI_SOCKET` → Rust Core `EventStream` → typed `get_workspaces` JSON-RPC →
GTK WebKit bridge → Svelte. Workspace IDs are strings (safe for Niri's u64),
and focus, visibility and urgency are separate flags. Clicking a workspace
chip sends only the validated Niri `FocusWorkspace` action by stable ID;
keyboard shortcuts continue to work independently.

With no Niri IPC connection, the UI shows `NIRI OFFLINE` instead of fake
workspaces. The Core reconnects automatically after disconnection.
A persistent read-only Core→Shell subscription now pushes changed workspace
snapshots as typed WebKit `kira:workspaces` events, so the Svelte UI updates
without the old 1.5-second polling delay.

To test the actual Niri workspace integration without modifying the host:

```sh
nix develop --command task qa:visual:fast
```

The QA smoke now waits for a workspace snapshot from the child compositor
through Core, in addition to the existing WebKit/Svelte verification. This
does not capture the screen or copy to the clipboard. Read more in
[the development guide](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md#read-only-niri-workspaces-stage-1-first-increment).

## Visual QA before Niri IPC integration

Run **read-only** packaged Niri/Core/Svelte smoke on a graphical
NixOS/Wayland session (no screenshots, scale changes or clipboard writes):

```sh
nix develop --command task qa:visual:release
```

To **explicitly opt in** to capturing 100%, 125%, 150% and 200% scales:

```sh
nix develop --command task qa:visual:capture:release
```

Capture uses `grim` bound to the nested Wayland display, **not** the Niri
screenshot action (which also copies to clipboard). PNGs and manifests are
stored locally in ignored `artifacts/visual-qa/`. Automated capture and CI
are not substitutes for a real visual review. See
[visual QA guide](docs/QA_VISUAL.md) for scope and acceptance criteria.

## Current limitations

The panel communicates with Core through typed IPC, shows live Niri workspaces and supports a narrowly scoped mouse-focus action. Full KDL grammar, custom theme loading, docks and third-party widgets remain future milestones.

This project is not ready to replace a working desktop environment.

FILE	Taskfile.yml
version: '3'

tasks:
  default:
    desc: Run all fast CI checks.
    cmds:
      - task: check

  check:
    desc: Validate structure, Core/IPC and frontend (native GTK shell checked separately).
    cmds:
      - task: spec:check
      - task: fmt
      - task: lint
      - task: test
      - task: config:check

  config:check:
    desc: Validate the sample KDL 2.0 config with the actual Core CLI.
    cmds:
      - cargo run --locked -p kira-core -- --check-config "{{.ROOT_DIR}}/config/kira.kdl.example"

  spec:check:
    desc: Validate required documentation and infrastructure.
    cmds:
      - test -s README.md
      - test -s docs/SPECIFICATION.md
      - test -s docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
      - test -s frontend/src/lib/themes/kira-default.css
      - test -s frontend/src/lib/themes/kira-default.ts
      - test -s frontend/src/style.css
      - test -s frontend/vite.config.ts
      - test -s docs/DEVELOPMENT.md
      - test -s Cargo.toml
      - test -s crates/kira-ipc/src/lib.rs
      - test -s crates/kira-core/src/main.rs
      - test -s crates/kira-shell/src/main.rs
      - test -s frontend/package.json
      - test -s flake.nix
      - test -s nix/package.nix
      - test -s Taskfile.yml
      - test -s .github/workflows/ci.yml
      - test -s scripts/dev_preview.py
      - test -s docs/PREVIEW.md
      - test -s docs/CONFIG.md
      - test -s config/kira.kdl.example
      - test -s crates/kira-core/src/config.rs

  fmt:
    desc: Check formatting of all Rust crates.
    cmds:
      - cargo fmt --all -- --check

  lint:
    desc: Lint Core/IPC and check Svelte/TypeScript.
    cmds:
      - cargo clippy --locked -p kira-ipc -p kira-core --all-targets -- -D warnings
      - npm run check --prefix frontend

  test:
    desc: Run Core/IPC and frontend tests.
    cmds:
      - cargo test --locked -p kira-ipc -p kira-core --all-targets
      - npm run test:ci --prefix frontend
      - python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_*.py'

  shell:check:
    desc: Check GTK Shell using the native libraries provided by nix develop.
    cmds:
      - cargo check --locked -p kira-shell

  frontend:deps:
    desc: Install locked frontend dependencies only when they change.
    cmds:
      - |
        current="$(sha256sum frontend/package-lock.json | cut -d ' ' -f 1)"
        stamp="frontend/node_modules/.kira-package-lock.sha256"
        if [ ! -x frontend/node_modules/.bin/vite ] || [ ! -f "$stamp" ] || [ "$(cat "$stamp")" != "$current" ]; then
          npm ci --prefix frontend --no-audit --no-fund
          printf '%s' "$current" > "$stamp"
        fi

  frontend:install:
    desc: Install locked frontend dependencies, regardless of cache.
    cmds:
      - npm ci --prefix frontend --no-audit --no-fund

  frontend:dev:
    desc: Run Vite for frontend development.
    cmds:
      - npm run dev --prefix frontend

  frontend:build:
    desc: Build production Svelte assets.
    cmds:
      - npm run build --prefix frontend

  core:run:
    desc: Run the Rust Core daemon.
    cmds:
      - cargo run -p kira-core

  shell:run:
    desc: Build frontend and run GTK layer-shell under Niri.
    cmds:
      - task: frontend:build
      - cargo run -p kira-shell

  build:
    desc: Build both layers and all Rust binaries.
    cmds:
      - task: frontend:build
      - cargo build --locked --release --workspace

  dev:preview:
    desc: Fast nested Niri preview using cached Cargo debug builds and Vite assets.
    cmds:
      - task: frontend:deps
      - task: frontend:build
      - cargo build --locked -p kira-core -p kira-shell
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --bin-dir target/debug --ui-dir frontend/dist

  dev:preview:run:
    desc: Reopen preview with already built debug binaries and UI assets.
    cmds:
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --bin-dir target/debug --ui-dir frontend/dist

  dev:preview:debug:
    desc: Reopen existing preview and stream WebKit/JavaScript logs without compiling.
    cmds:
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --bin-dir target/debug --ui-dir frontend/dist --debug

  dev:preview:release:
    desc: Verify the full Nix package in a nested Niri compositor.
    cmds:
      - task: nix:build
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py

  dev:preview:test:
    desc: Test nested preview safety and lifecycle without a running Niri.
    cmds:
      - python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_*.py' -v

  qa:visual:fast:
    desc: Run read-only Core/Svelte/Niri smoke in nested debug preview; no screenshots or scale changes.
    cmds:
      - task: frontend:deps
      - task: frontend:build
      - cargo build --locked -p kira-core -p kira-shell
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --bin-dir target/debug --ui-dir frontend/dist --qa-smoke

  qa:visual:release:
    desc: Run read-only Core/Svelte/Niri smoke using the real Nix package; no screenshots.
    cmds:
      - task: nix:build
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --qa-smoke

  qa:visual:capture:fast:
    desc: OPT-IN four scale screenshots via grim in isolated debug preview (no clipboard).
    cmds:
      - task: frontend:deps
      - task: frontend:build
      - cargo build --locked -p kira-core -p kira-shell
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --bin-dir target/debug --ui-dir frontend/dist --qa-output-dir artifacts/visual-qa

  qa:visual:capture:release:
    desc: OPT-IN four scale PNGs via grim from packaged Nix Shell (no clipboard).
    cmds:
      - task: nix:build
      - python3 scripts/dev_preview.py --qa-output-dir artifacts/visual-qa

  nix:check:
    desc: Check the Nix flake.
    cmds:
      - nix flake check

  nix:build:
    desc: Build the package when real lock files and hashes are added.
    cmds:
      - |
        if [ ! -f Cargo.lock ] || [ ! -f frontend/package-lock.json ] || [ ! -f flake.lock ]; then
          echo "Missing lock files. Generate and commit real Cargo, npm and Nix locks first."
          exit 1
        fi
      - nix build .#default

FILE	config/kira.kdl.example
// Kira Desktop settings, supported strict KDL profile (not Niri's config).
// Place in ~/.config/kira-desktop/config.kdl, or pass KIRA_CONFIG_FILE=/absolute/path.
// All values below are the defaults. Changes are picked up automatically.
kira {
    bar compact=#false title="KIRA DESKTOP"
    clock seconds=#false
    workspaces show-names=#true limit=12
}

FILE	crates/kira-core/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "kira-core"
version.workspace = true
edition.workspace = true
license.workspace = true

[dependencies]
kira-ipc = { path = "../kira-ipc" }
serde_json.workspace = true
tokio.workspace = true

FILE	crates/kira-core/src/config.rs
//! Strict, deliberately small KDL configuration profile for the first MVP.
//! No arbitrary commands, includes, environment interpolation or KDL actions.
//! A rejected update leaves the last successfully parsed configuration active.

use std::collections::HashSet;
use std::io::{self, Read};
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
use std::time::Duration;

use kira_ipc::{ConfigState, UiConfig};
use tokio::sync::watch;

const MAX_CONFIG_BYTES: u64 = 64 * 1024;
const MAX_LINES: usize = 128;

/// No user configuration file is created or overwritten by the daemon.
/// KIRA_CONFIG_FILE must be absolute, including in the isolated preview.
pub fn config_path() -> Result<PathBuf, String> {
    if let Some(override_path) = std::env::var_os("KIRA_CONFIG_FILE") {
        let path = PathBuf::from(override_path);
        return if path.is_absolute() {
            Ok(path)
        } else {
            Err("KIRA_CONFIG_FILE must be an absolute path".into())
        };
    }
    if let Some(xdg) = std::env::var_os("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") {
        let path = PathBuf::from(xdg);
        return if path.is_absolute() {
            Ok(path.join("kira-desktop/config.kdl"))
        } else {
            Err("XDG_CONFIG_HOME must be an absolute path".into())
        };
    }
    let home = std::env::var_os("HOME").ok_or("HOME is not set")?;
    let home = PathBuf::from(home);
    if !home.is_absolute() {
        return Err("HOME must be an absolute path".into());
    }
    Ok(home.join(".config/kira-desktop/config.kdl"))
}

/// Truncate comments only outside quoted strings; values may contain "//".
fn strip_comment(line: &str) -> &str {
    let mut quoted = false;
    let mut escaped = false;
    let mut previous_slash = None;
    for (index, ch) in line.char_indices() {
        if quoted {
            if escaped {
                escaped = false;
            } else if ch == '\\' {
                escaped = true;
            } else if ch == '"' {
                quoted = false;
            }
        } else if ch == '"' {
            quoted = true;
        } else if ch == '/' {
            if let Some(start) = previous_slash {
                return &line[..start];
            }
            previous_slash = Some(index);
            continue;
        }
        previous_slash = None;
    }
    line
}

/// Tokens are node names and key=value properties. Quoted JSON-style strings
/// may contain spaces, backslashes and "=", but nodes remain one per line.
fn line_tokens(line: &str) -> Result<Vec<String>, String> {
    let mut result = Vec::new();
    let mut token = String::new();
    let mut quoted = false;
    let mut escaped = false;
    for ch in line.chars() {
        if quoted {
            token.push(ch);
            if escaped {
                escaped = false;
            } else if ch == '\\' {
                escaped = true;
            } else if ch == '"' {
                quoted = false;
            }
        } else if ch == '"' {
            quoted = true;
            token.push(ch);
        } else if ch.is_whitespace() {
            if !token.is_empty() {
                result.push(std::mem::take(&mut token));
            }
        } else {
            token.push(ch);
        }
    }
    if quoted {
        return Err("unterminated quoted string".into());
    }
    if !token.is_empty() {
        result.push(token);
    }
    Ok(result)
}

/// The first profile accepts quoted titles with only the two shared
/// KDL 2.0/JSON escapes needed for visible text: \\" and \\\\.
/// JSON's \\uNNNN and \\/ forms are not valid KDL 2.0 string escapes.
fn title_literal(raw: &str) -> Result<String, String> {
    let mut escaped = false;
    for character in raw.chars() {
        if escaped {
            if !matches!(character, '"' | '\\') {
                return Err("unsupported quoted-string escape in bar.title".into());
            }
            escaped = false;
        } else if character == '\\' {
            escaped = true;
        }
    }
    serde_json::from_str(raw).map_err(|_| "bar.title must be a quoted string".into())
}

fn boolean(value: &str, key: &str) -> Result<bool, String> {
    match value {
        "#true" => Ok(true),
        "#false" => Ok(false),
        _ => Err(format!("{key} must be #true or #false")),
    }
}

/// Parse only the documented, valid KDL subset. Reject unknown nodes,
/// duplicate properties and unsafe or unsupported syntax instead of guessing.
pub fn parse(input: &str) -> Result<UiConfig, String> {
    if input.len() as u64 > MAX_CONFIG_BYTES {
        return Err("config exceeds 64 KiB".into());
    }
    if input.lines().count() > MAX_LINES {
        return Err("config exceeds 128 lines".into());
    }

    let mut config = UiConfig::default();
    let mut root_open = false;
    let mut root_closed = false;
    let mut seen_nodes = HashSet::new();

    for (number, raw_line) in input.lines().enumerate() {
        let line = strip_comment(raw_line).trim();
        if line.is_empty() {
            continue;
        }
        if !root_open {
            if line != "kira {" {
                return Err(format!("line {}: expected 'kira {{'", number + 1));
            }
            root_open = true;
            continue;
        }
        if root_closed {
            return Err(format!(
                "line {}: unexpected content after kira block",
                number + 1
            ));
        }
        if line == "}" {
            root_closed = true;
            continue;
        }

        let tokens = line_tokens(line).map_err(|e| format!("line {}: {e}", number + 1))?;
        let node = tokens.first().map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("");
        if !matches!(node, "bar" | "clock" | "workspaces") {
            return Err(format!("line {}: unknown KDL node '{node}'", number + 1));
        }
        if !seen_nodes.insert(node.to_owned()) {
            return Err(format!("line {}: duplicate node '{node}'", number + 1));
        }
        let mut seen_properties = HashSet::new();
        for prop in tokens.iter().skip(1) {
            let Some((key, raw_value)) = prop.split_once('=') else {
                return Err(format!("line {}: expected key=value property", number + 1));
            };
            if key.is_empty() || raw_value.is_empty() {
                return Err(format!("line {}: empty property name or value", number + 1));
            }
            if !seen_properties.insert(key) {
                return Err(format!("line {}: duplicate property '{key}'", number + 1));
            }
            let key_path = format!("{node}.{key}");
            match (node, key) {
                ("bar", "compact") => config.compact = boolean(raw_value, &key_path)?,
                ("bar", "title") => {
                    let title = title_literal(raw_value)
                        .map_err(|e| format!("line {}: {e}", number + 1))?;
                    if title.is_empty()
                        || title.chars().count() > 32
                        || title.chars().any(char::is_control)
                    {
                        return Err(format!(
                            "line {}: bar.title must contain 1–32 printable characters",
                            number + 1
                        ));
                    }
                    config.title = title;
                }
                ("clock", "seconds") => config.show_seconds = boolean(raw_value, &key_path)?,
                ("workspaces", "show-names") => config.show_names = boolean(raw_value, &key_path)?,
                ("workspaces", "limit") => {
                    let limit = raw_value.parse::<u8>().map_err(|_| {
                        format!("line {}: workspaces.limit must be an integer", number + 1)
                    })?;
                    if !(1..=32).contains(&limit) {
                        return Err(format!(
                            "line {}: workspaces.limit must be 1–32",
                            number + 1
                        ));
                    }
                    config.max_workspaces = limit;
                }
                _ => {
                    return Err(format!(
                        "line {}: unsupported property '{key_path}'",
                        number + 1
                    ));
                }
            }
        }
    }
    if !root_open || !root_closed {
        return Err("expected one closed kira { ... } block".into());
    }
    Ok(config)
}

pub fn load(path: &Path) -> Result<UiConfig, String> {
    let file = std::fs::File::open(path).map_err(|e| format!("cannot read config: {e}"))?;
    let mut bytes = Vec::new();
    file.take(MAX_CONFIG_BYTES + 1)
        .read_to_end(&mut bytes)
        .map_err(|e| format!("cannot read config: {e}"))?;
    if bytes.len() as u64 > MAX_CONFIG_BYTES {
        return Err("config exceeds 64 KiB".into());
    }
    let text = std::str::from_utf8(&bytes).map_err(|_| "config must be UTF-8".to_string())?;
    parse(text)
}

fn apply(current: &ConfigState, latest: Result<UiConfig, String>) -> ConfigState {
    match latest {
        Ok(config) => ConfigState {
            config,
            error: None,
        },
        Err(error) => ConfigState {
            config: current.config.clone(),
            error: Some(error),
        },
    }
}

/// Poll the small user-owned file at most four times per second.
/// Compare contents/state and publish only changes; atomic rename is detected.
/// Missing file on first startup means defaults. Removing a previously valid
/// file is treated as an error and retains the last valid state.
pub async fn monitor(path: PathBuf, sender: watch::Sender<ConfigState>) {
    let mut initialized = false;
    let mut previous_contents: Option<Result<Vec<u8>, io::ErrorKind>> = None;
    loop {
        // Hard cap the read itself, even for a huge or growing file.
        let current = std::fs::File::open(&path)
            .and_then(|file| {
                let mut bytes = Vec::new();
                file.take(MAX_CONFIG_BYTES + 1).read_to_end(&mut bytes)?;
                if bytes.len() as u64 > MAX_CONFIG_BYTES {
                    Err(io::Error::new(
                        io::ErrorKind::InvalidData,
                        "config too large",
                    ))
                } else {
                    Ok(bytes)
                }
            })
            .map_err(|error| error.kind());

        // Don't reparse unchanged contents, but still catch atomic replacements.
        let changed = match (&previous_contents, &current) {
            (Some(Ok(old)), Ok(new)) => old != new,
            (Some(Err(old)), Err(new)) => old != new,
            _ => true,
        };
        if changed {
            let state = if !initialized && matches!(&current, Err(io::ErrorKind::NotFound)) {
                ConfigState::default()
            } else {
                let parsed = match &current {
                    Ok(bytes) => std::str::from_utf8(bytes)
                        .map_err(|_| "config must be UTF-8".to_owned())
                        .and_then(parse),
                    Err(io::ErrorKind::InvalidData) => Err("config exceeds 64 KiB".into()),
                    Err(error) => Err(format!("cannot read config: {error}")),
                };
                apply(&sender.borrow().clone(), parsed)
            };
            if *sender.borrow() != state {
                if let Some(error) = &state.error {
                    eprintln!("kira-core config: {error}; keeping previous valid settings");
                }
                sender.send_replace(state);
            }
            previous_contents = Some(current);
            initialized = true;
        }
        tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(250)).await;
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    const EXAMPLE: &str = include_str!("../../../config/kira.kdl.example");

    #[test]
    fn example_parses_and_uses_defaults() {
        assert_eq!(parse(EXAMPLE).unwrap(), UiConfig::default());
        assert_eq!(parse("kira {\n  bar compact=#true title=\"KIRA // TEST\"\n  clock seconds=#true\n  workspaces show-names=#false limit=3\n}\n").unwrap(),
            UiConfig { compact: true, title: "KIRA // TEST".into(), show_seconds: true,
                show_names: false, max_workspaces: 3 });
    }

    #[test]
    fn invalid_config_cannot_override_previous_valid_state() {
        let initial = ConfigState {
            config: parse("kira {\n  bar compact=#true\n}\n").unwrap(),
            error: None,
        };
        for broken in [
            "kira {\n  bar compact=#false\n  bar compact=#true\n}",
            "kira {\n  workspaces limit=0\n}",
            "kira {\n  clock seconds=yes\n}",
            "kira {\n  bar title=\"\"\n}",
            "kira {\n  bar title=\"bad\\nnewline\"\n}",
            "kira {\n  exec command=\"rm -rf\"\n}",
            "kira {\n  bar compact=#true compact=#false\n}",
            "kira {\n  workspaces limit=99\n}",
            "kira {\n  clock seconds=#true",
            "kira { }\n",
            "kira {\n  clock seconds=true\n}\n", // KDL v1 boolean is not KDL 2.0
            "kira {\n  bar title=\"\\u0041\"\n}\n", // JSON-only escape is invalid KDL2
            "kira {\n  bar title=\"\\/bad\"\n}\n",
        ] {
            assert!(parse(broken).is_err(), "{broken}");
            let next = apply(&initial, parse(broken));
            assert_eq!(next.config, initial.config);
            assert!(next.error.is_some());
        }
        assert!(apply(&initial, parse(EXAMPLE)).error.is_none());
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn hot_reload_rejects_invalid_and_recovers_from_atomic_replace() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("kira-kdl-{}", std::process::id()));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("config.kdl");
        let (tx, mut rx) = watch::channel(ConfigState::default());
        let task = tokio::spawn(monitor(path.clone(), tx));
        std::fs::write(&path, "kira {\n  clock seconds=#true\n}\n").unwrap();
        tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2), rx.changed())
            .await
            .unwrap()
            .unwrap();
        assert!(rx.borrow().config.show_seconds);
        std::fs::write(&path, "kira {\n  clock seconds=bad\n}\n").unwrap();
        tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2), rx.changed())
            .await
            .unwrap()
            .unwrap();
        assert!(rx.borrow().config.show_seconds);
        assert!(rx.borrow().error.is_some());
        let staged = directory.join("pending.kdl");
        std::fs::write(&staged, "kira {\n  clock seconds=#false\n}\n").unwrap();
        std::fs::rename(staged, &path).unwrap();
        tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2), rx.changed())
            .await
            .unwrap()
            .unwrap();
        assert!(!rx.borrow().config.show_seconds);
        assert!(rx.borrow().error.is_none());
        task.abort();
        std::fs::remove_file(path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn relative_path_never_falls_back_to_host_config() {
        assert!(Path::new("config.kdl").is_relative());
    }
}

FILE	crates/kira-core/src/main.rs
//! Core state daemon: read-only subscriptions plus one checked Niri focus action.

mod config;
mod niri;

use std::error::Error;
use std::fs::{self, File, OpenOptions};
use std::io;
use std::os::unix::fs::{FileTypeExt, MetadataExt, OpenOptionsExt, PermissionsExt};
use std::os::unix::net::UnixStream as StdUnixStream;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

use kira_ipc::{ConfigState, RpcRequest, RpcResponse, WorkspaceState, dispatch_with_state};
use tokio::io::{AsyncBufRead, AsyncBufReadExt, AsyncWriteExt, BufReader};
use tokio::net::{UnixListener, UnixStream};
use tokio::sync::watch;

const MAX_REQUEST_BYTES: usize = 4096;

/// Delete only the socket inode owned by this Core instance.
struct SocketGuard {
    path: PathBuf,
    device: u64,
    inode: u64,
}

impl SocketGuard {
    fn new(path: &Path) -> io::Result<Self> {
        let metadata = std::fs::symlink_metadata(path)?;
        if !metadata.file_type().is_socket() {
            return Err(io::Error::new(
                io::ErrorKind::InvalidData,
                "Not a Unix socket",
            ));
        }
        Ok(Self {
            path: path.to_owned(),
            device: metadata.dev(),
            inode: metadata.ino(),
        })
    }
}

impl Drop for SocketGuard {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        let Ok(metadata) = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&self.path) else {
            return;
        };
        if metadata.file_type().is_socket()
            && metadata.dev() == self.device
            && metadata.ino() == self.inode
            && let Err(error) = std::fs::remove_file(&self.path)
        {
            eprintln!("kira-core: cannot remove owned socket: {error}");
        }
    }
}

/// Only replace an abandoned socket, never a live daemon or another file.
/// The sidecar lock serializes cooperating Core instances during recovery.
/// Keep the lock file on disk: unlinking a locked file permits a second lock
/// on a new inode. The enclosing runtime/preview directory owns its cleanup.
fn recover_stale_socket(path: &Path, lock: &File) -> io::Result<()> {
    let occupied = |reason: &'static str| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::AddrInUse, reason);
    let parent = path
        .parent()
        .ok_or_else(|| occupied("Core socket has no parent directory"))?;
    let directory = fs::symlink_metadata(parent)?;
    let socket = fs::symlink_metadata(path)?;
    let owner = lock.metadata()?.uid();

    // Automatic deletion is allowed only in a private, same-owner directory.
    // symlink_metadata prevents a socket-path symlink from being followed.
    if !directory.file_type().is_dir()
        || directory.permissions().mode() & 0o022 != 0
        || directory.uid() != owner
        || !socket.file_type().is_socket()
        || socket.uid() != owner
    {
        return Err(occupied(
            "Refusing to replace Core socket outside a private, owner-matched directory",
        ));
    }

    match StdUnixStream::connect(path) {
        Ok(_) => return Err(occupied("Another Core is listening on the socket")),
        Err(error) if error.kind() == io::ErrorKind::ConnectionRefused => {}
        Err(error) => return Err(error), // PermissionDenied/other errors are not proof of staleness.
    }

    // Detect a replacement between the probe and unlink. Together with the
    // sidecar lock this prevents concurrent Core startups from deleting each
    // other's freshly bound sockets.
    let current = fs::symlink_metadata(path)?;
    if !current.file_type().is_socket()
        || current.dev() != socket.dev()
        || current.ino() != socket.ino()
    {
        return Err(occupied("Core socket changed during stale-socket recovery"));
    }
    fs::remove_file(path)?;
    eprintln!("kira-core: removed abandoned socket {}", path.display());
    Ok(())
}

/// Bind normally, or retry once after verified stale-socket cleanup.
/// The returned lock must live for as long as the listener is running.
fn bind_core_socket(path: &Path) -> io::Result<(File, SocketGuard, UnixListener)> {
    let mut lock_path = path.as_os_str().to_os_string();
    lock_path.push(".lock");
    let lock = OpenOptions::new()
        .read(true)
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .truncate(false) // Persist the inode shared by future Core startups.
        .mode(0o600)
        .open(PathBuf::from(lock_path))?;
    lock.try_lock().map_err(|error| {
        io::Error::new(
            io::ErrorKind::AddrInUse,
            format!("Another Core holds the socket startup lock: {error}"),
        )
    })?;

    let listener = match UnixListener::bind(path) {
        Ok(listener) => listener,
        Err(error) if error.kind() == io::ErrorKind::AddrInUse => {
            recover_stale_socket(path, &lock)?;
            UnixListener::bind(path)?
        }
        Err(error) => return Err(error),
    };
    let guard = SocketGuard::new(path)?;
    // Pattern bindings drop in reverse order: listener, guard, then lock.
    Ok((lock, guard, listener))
}

/// Read newline-delimited IPC without growing beyond the configured bound.
async fn read_bounded_line<R: AsyncBufRead + Unpin>(
    reader: &mut R,
    max_bytes: usize,
) -> io::Result<Option<Vec<u8>>> {
    let mut line = Vec::new();
    loop {
        let buffer = reader.fill_buf().await?;
        if buffer.is_empty() {
            return if line.is_empty() {
                Ok(None)
            } else {
                Err(io::Error::new(
                    io::ErrorKind::UnexpectedEof,
                    "Incomplete IPC request",
                ))
            };
        }
        let count = buffer
            .iter()
            .position(|byte| *byte == b'\n')
            .map_or(buffer.len(), |position| position + 1);
        if count > max_bytes.saturating_sub(line.len()) {
            return Err(io::Error::new(
                io::ErrorKind::InvalidData,
                "IPC request too large",
            ));
        }
        line.extend_from_slice(&buffer[..count]);
        let complete = buffer[count - 1] == b'\n';
        reader.consume(count);
        if complete {
            return Ok(Some(line));
        }
    }
}

/// Serialize each subscription frame with the original JSON-RPC id.
async fn send_subscription_frame(
    writer: &mut tokio::net::unix::OwnedWriteHalf,
    frame: RpcResponse,
) -> io::Result<()> {
    writer.write_all(&serde_json::to_vec(&frame)?).await?;
    writer.write_all(b"\n").await
}

/// Keep subscriptions healthy when Niri has no new events. A heartbeat is a
/// distinct frame, never a repeated workspace state or a JS-visible event.
async fn stream_workspaces_with_heartbeat(
    writer: &mut tokio::net::unix::OwnedWriteHalf,
    mut workspaces: watch::Receiver<WorkspaceState>,
    id: u64,
    heartbeat_every: std::time::Duration,
) -> io::Result<()> {
    let snapshot = workspaces.borrow_and_update().clone();
    send_subscription_frame(
        writer,
        RpcResponse::success(id, serde_json::to_value(snapshot)?),
    )
    .await?;
    let mut heartbeat = tokio::time::interval_at(
        tokio::time::Instant::now() + heartbeat_every,
        heartbeat_every,
    );
    heartbeat.set_missed_tick_behavior(tokio::time::MissedTickBehavior::Skip);
    loop {
        tokio::select! {
            changed = workspaces.changed() => {
                if changed.is_err() {
                    return Ok(());
                }
                let snapshot = workspaces.borrow_and_update().clone();
                send_subscription_frame(
                    writer,
                    RpcResponse::success(id, serde_json::to_value(snapshot)?),
                ).await?;
            }
            _ = heartbeat.tick() => {
                send_subscription_frame(writer, RpcResponse::heartbeat(id)).await?;
            }
        }
    }
}

async fn stream_workspaces(
    writer: &mut tokio::net::unix::OwnedWriteHalf,
    workspaces: watch::Receiver<WorkspaceState>,
    id: u64,
) -> io::Result<()> {
    stream_workspaces_with_heartbeat(
        writer,
        workspaces,
        id,
        kira_ipc::SUBSCRIPTION_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL,
    )
    .await
}

/// Internal config stream also sends heartbeats without changing its last
/// known good settings. No KDL validation or disk IO occurs on heartbeats.
async fn stream_config_with_heartbeat(
    writer: &mut tokio::net::unix::OwnedWriteHalf,
    mut config: watch::Receiver<ConfigState>,
    id: u64,
    heartbeat_every: std::time::Duration,
) -> io::Result<()> {
    let snapshot = config.borrow_and_update().clone();
    send_subscription_frame(
        writer,
        RpcResponse::success(id, serde_json::to_value(snapshot)?),
    )
    .await?;
    let mut heartbeat = tokio::time::interval_at(
        tokio::time::Instant::now() + heartbeat_every,
        heartbeat_every,
    );
    heartbeat.set_missed_tick_behavior(tokio::time::MissedTickBehavior::Skip);
    loop {
        tokio::select! {
            changed = config.changed() => {
                if changed.is_err() {
                    return Ok(());
                }
                let snapshot = config.borrow_and_update().clone();
                send_subscription_frame(
                    writer,
                    RpcResponse::success(id, serde_json::to_value(snapshot)?),
                ).await?;
            }
            _ = heartbeat.tick() => {
                send_subscription_frame(writer, RpcResponse::heartbeat(id)).await?;
            }
        }
    }
}

async fn stream_config(
    writer: &mut tokio::net::unix::OwnedWriteHalf,
    config: watch::Receiver<ConfigState>,
    id: u64,
) -> io::Result<()> {
    stream_config_with_heartbeat(
        writer,
        config,
        id,
        kira_ipc::SUBSCRIPTION_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL,
    )
    .await
}

async fn serve(
    stream: UnixStream,
    workspaces: watch::Receiver<WorkspaceState>,
    config: watch::Receiver<ConfigState>,
    niri_socket: Option<&Path>,
) -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync>> {
    let (read_half, mut writer) = stream.into_split();
    let mut reader = BufReader::new(read_half);

    while let Some(line) = read_bounded_line(&mut reader, MAX_REQUEST_BYTES).await? {
        let response = match serde_json::from_slice::<RpcRequest>(&line) {
            Ok(request)
                if request.method == "subscribe_workspaces"
                    && request.jsonrpc == kira_ipc::PROTOCOL_VERSION =>
            {
                // Internal streaming endpoint, not exposed through the WebKit
                // JS RPC allowlist; one subscription per socket connection.
                return Ok(stream_workspaces(&mut writer, workspaces, request.id).await?);
            }
            Ok(request)
                if request.method == "subscribe_config"
                    && request.jsonrpc == kira_ipc::PROTOCOL_VERSION =>
            {
                return Ok(stream_config(&mut writer, config, request.id).await?);
            }
            Ok(request)
                if request.method == "focus_workspace"
                    && request.jsonrpc == kira_ipc::PROTOCOL_VERSION =>
            {
                // This is intentionally the sole Niri mutation available
                // through Core. The ID must exist in a connected snapshot.
                let state = workspaces.borrow().clone();
                match niri::validated_focus_id(request.params.as_ref(), &state) {
                    Err(message) => RpcResponse::failure(Some(request.id), -32602, message),
                    Ok(id) => match niri_socket {
                        Some(path) => match niri::focus_workspace(path, id).await {
                            Ok(()) => RpcResponse::success(
                                request.id,
                                serde_json::json!({"accepted": true}),
                            ),
                            Err(error) => {
                                eprintln!("kira-core: Niri workspace focus failed: {error}");
                                RpcResponse::failure(
                                    Some(request.id),
                                    -32000,
                                    "Niri workspace focus failed",
                                )
                            }
                        },
                        None => RpcResponse::failure(Some(request.id), -32000, "Niri unavailable"),
                    },
                }
            }
            Ok(request) => dispatch_with_state(
                request,
                &workspaces.borrow().clone(),
                &config.borrow().clone(),
            ),
            Err(_) => RpcResponse::failure(None, -32700, "Parse error"),
        };
        let encoded = serde_json::to_vec(&response)?;
        writer.write_all(&encoded).await?;
        writer.write_all(b"\n").await?;
    }
    Ok(())
}

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> {
    // Pure validation command: no GUI, Core socket or compositor required.
    let mut args = std::env::args_os().skip(1);
    if let Some(option) = args.next() {
        if option != "--check-config" {
            return Err("Usage: kira-core [--check-config /absolute/path/config.kdl]".into());
        }
        let path = args.next().ok_or("--check-config requires a file path")?;
        if args.next().is_some() {
            return Err("--check-config accepts exactly one file path".into());
        }
        let path = PathBuf::from(path);
        if !path.is_absolute() {
            return Err("--check-config requires an absolute path".into());
        }
        let settings = config::load(&path).map_err(io::Error::other)?;
        println!("{}", serde_json::to_string_pretty(&settings)?);
        return Ok(());
    }

    let path = kira_ipc::core_socket_path()?;
    // Reclaim only a verified abandoned socket; preserve live Core instances.
    let (_socket_lock, _guard, listener) = bind_core_socket(&path)?;
    eprintln!("kira-core listening on {}", path.display());

    let (config_sender, config_receiver) = watch::channel(ConfigState::default());
    match config::config_path() {
        Ok(path) => {
            eprintln!("kira-core: watching KDL config at {}", path.display());
            tokio::spawn(config::monitor(path, config_sender));
        }
        Err(error) => {
            config_sender.send_replace(ConfigState {
                config: Default::default(),
                error: Some(error),
            });
        }
    }

    let (workspace_sender, workspace_receiver) = watch::channel(WorkspaceState::default());
    let niri_socket = niri::socket_path_from(std::env::var_os("NIRI_SOCKET"));
    if let Some(socket) = niri_socket.clone() {
        tokio::spawn(niri::monitor(socket, workspace_sender.clone()));
    } else {
        eprintln!("kira-core: no valid NIRI_SOCKET; workspace state will be offline");
    }

    let mut terminate = tokio::signal::unix::signal(tokio::signal::unix::SignalKind::terminate())?;
    loop {
        tokio::select! {
            accepted = listener.accept() => {
                let (stream, _) = accepted?;
                let state = workspace_receiver.clone();
                let config = config_receiver.clone();
                let socket = niri_socket.clone();
                tokio::spawn(async move {
                    if let Err(error) = serve(stream, state, config, socket.as_deref()).await {
                        eprintln!("kira-core client error: {error}");
                    }
                });
            }
            _ = tokio::signal::ctrl_c() => break,
            _ = terminate.recv() => break,
        }
    }
    eprintln!("kira-core shutting down");
    Ok(())
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn quiet_workspace_stream_emits_heartbeat_without_replaying_state() {
        use tokio::io::AsyncBufReadExt;
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-heartbeat-ws-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("ipc.sock");
        let listener = UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let (_tx, rx) = watch::channel(WorkspaceState::default());
        let server = tokio::spawn(async move {
            let (stream, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
            let (_, mut writer) = stream.into_split();
            stream_workspaces_with_heartbeat(
                &mut writer,
                rx,
                91,
                std::time::Duration::from_millis(30),
            )
            .await
            .unwrap();
        });
        let stream = UnixStream::connect(&path).await.unwrap();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(stream);
        let mut first = String::new();
        let mut heartbeat = String::new();
        tokio::time::timeout(std::time::Duration::from_secs(1), async {
            reader.read_line(&mut first).await.unwrap();
            reader.read_line(&mut heartbeat).await.unwrap();
        })
        .await
        .unwrap();
        let snapshot: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&first).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(snapshot.id, Some(91));
        assert_eq!(snapshot.result.unwrap()["connected"], false);
        let beat: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&heartbeat).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(beat.id, Some(91));
        assert!(kira_ipc::is_subscription_heartbeat(
            beat.result.as_ref().unwrap()
        ));
        server.abort();
        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn quiet_config_stream_emits_heartbeat_without_config_change() {
        use tokio::io::AsyncBufReadExt;
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-heartbeat-config-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("ipc.sock");
        let listener = UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let (_tx, rx) = watch::channel(ConfigState::default());
        let server = tokio::spawn(async move {
            let (stream, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
            let (_, mut writer) = stream.into_split();
            stream_config_with_heartbeat(&mut writer, rx, 92, std::time::Duration::from_millis(30))
                .await
                .unwrap();
        });
        let stream = UnixStream::connect(&path).await.unwrap();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(stream);
        let mut first = String::new();
        let mut heartbeat = String::new();
        tokio::time::timeout(std::time::Duration::from_secs(1), async {
            reader.read_line(&mut first).await.unwrap();
            reader.read_line(&mut heartbeat).await.unwrap();
        })
        .await
        .unwrap();
        let snapshot: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&first).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(snapshot.id, Some(92));
        assert_eq!(snapshot.result.unwrap()["config"]["compact"], false);
        let beat: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&heartbeat).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(beat.id, Some(92));
        assert!(kira_ipc::is_subscription_heartbeat(
            beat.result.as_ref().unwrap()
        ));
        server.abort();
        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn bounded_reader_preserves_consecutive_messages() {
        let input = b"one\nnext\n".as_slice();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(input);
        assert_eq!(
            read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 8).await.unwrap(),
            Some(b"one\n".to_vec())
        );
        assert_eq!(
            read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 8).await.unwrap(),
            Some(b"next\n".to_vec())
        );
        assert_eq!(read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 8).await.unwrap(), None);
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn bounded_reader_rejects_long_requests() {
        let input = b"123456789\n".as_slice();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(input);
        let error = read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 8).await.unwrap_err();
        assert_eq!(error.kind(), io::ErrorKind::InvalidData);
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn bounded_reader_rejects_unterminated_requests() {
        let input = b"not-terminated".as_slice();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(input);
        let error = read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 32).await.unwrap_err();
        assert_eq!(error.kind(), io::ErrorKind::UnexpectedEof);
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn subscription_streams_initial_snapshot_and_focus_changes() {
        use tokio::io::{AsyncBufReadExt, BufReader as TokioBufReader};
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("kira-subscribe-{}", std::process::id()));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        let path = dir.join("ipc.sock");
        let listener = tokio::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let (tx, rx) = watch::channel(WorkspaceState::default());
        let task = tokio::spawn(async move {
            let (stream, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
            let (_tx_config, rx_config) = watch::channel(ConfigState::default());
            let _ = serve(stream, rx, rx_config, None).await;
        });
        let mut conn = UnixStream::connect(&path).await.unwrap();
        conn.write_all(b"{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":77,\"method\":\"subscribe_workspaces\"}\n")
            .await
            .unwrap();
        let mut reader = TokioBufReader::new(conn);
        let mut line = String::new();
        tokio::time::timeout(
            std::time::Duration::from_secs(1),
            reader.read_line(&mut line),
        )
        .await
        .unwrap()
        .unwrap();
        let first: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&line).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(first.id, Some(77));
        assert_eq!(first.result.unwrap()["connected"], false);
        let next = WorkspaceState {
            connected: true,
            workspaces: vec![kira_ipc::Workspace {
                id: "123".into(),
                idx: 2,
                name: None,
                output: Some("winit".into()),
                is_active: true,
                is_focused: true,
                is_urgent: false,
            }],
        };
        tx.send_replace(next);
        line.clear();
        tokio::time::timeout(
            std::time::Duration::from_secs(1),
            reader.read_line(&mut line),
        )
        .await
        .unwrap()
        .unwrap();
        let update: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&line).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(update.id, Some(77));
        assert_eq!(update.result.unwrap()["workspaces"][0]["idx"], 2);
        drop(reader);
        task.abort();
        std::fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(&dir).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn config_subscription_delivers_latest_valid_snapshot() {
        use tokio::io::AsyncBufReadExt;
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("kira-config-sub-{}", std::process::id()));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        let path = dir.join("core.sock");
        let listener = UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let (_ws_tx, ws_rx) = watch::channel(WorkspaceState::default());
        let (cfg_tx, cfg_rx) = watch::channel(ConfigState::default());
        let server = tokio::spawn(async move {
            let (stream, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
            let _ = serve(stream, ws_rx, cfg_rx, None).await;
        });
        let mut stream = UnixStream::connect(&path).await.unwrap();
        stream
            .write_all(b"{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":88,\"method\":\"subscribe_config\"}\n")
            .await
            .unwrap();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(stream);
        let mut first = String::new();
        tokio::time::timeout(
            std::time::Duration::from_secs(1),
            reader.read_line(&mut first),
        )
        .await
        .unwrap()
        .unwrap();
        let first: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&first).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(first.result.unwrap()["config"]["compact"], false);
        cfg_tx.send_replace(ConfigState {
            config: kira_ipc::UiConfig {
                compact: true,
                ..Default::default()
            },
            error: None,
        });
        let mut second = String::new();
        tokio::time::timeout(
            std::time::Duration::from_secs(1),
            reader.read_line(&mut second),
        )
        .await
        .unwrap()
        .unwrap();
        let second: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&second).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(second.result.unwrap()["config"]["compact"], true);
        server.abort();
        std::fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(&dir).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn focus_rpc_refuses_unknown_workspace_before_niri_action() {
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("kira-focus-rpc-{}", std::process::id()));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        let path = dir.join("core.sock");
        let listener = UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let (_ws_tx, ws_rx) = watch::channel(WorkspaceState::default());
        let (_cfg_tx, cfg_rx) = watch::channel(ConfigState::default());
        let server = tokio::spawn(async move {
            let (stream, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
            let _ = serve(stream, ws_rx, cfg_rx, None).await;
        });
        let mut stream = UnixStream::connect(&path).await.unwrap();
        stream.write_all(b"{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":77,\"method\":\"focus_workspace\",\"params\":{\"id\":\"9\"}}\n").await.unwrap();
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(stream);
        let mut line = String::new();
        tokio::time::timeout(
            std::time::Duration::from_secs(1),
            tokio::io::AsyncBufReadExt::read_line(&mut reader, &mut line),
        )
        .await
        .unwrap()
        .unwrap();
        let response: RpcResponse = serde_json::from_str(&line).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(response.error.unwrap().code, -32602);
        server.abort();
        std::fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(&dir).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn replaces_abandoned_socket_after_unclean_shutdown() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-stale-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        let old_listener = std::os::unix::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        drop(old_listener); // Simulate SIGKILL: the socket path survives.
        assert!(path.exists());

        let (lock, guard, listener) = bind_core_socket(&path).unwrap();
        assert!(StdUnixStream::connect(&path).is_ok());
        drop(listener);
        drop(guard);
        drop(lock);
        assert!(!path.exists());
        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn refuses_to_replace_live_socket() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-live-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        let (lock, guard, listener) = bind_core_socket(&path).unwrap();
        let before = fs::symlink_metadata(&path).unwrap();

        assert!(bind_core_socket(&path).is_err());
        let after = fs::symlink_metadata(&path).unwrap();
        assert_eq!((before.dev(), before.ino()), (after.dev(), after.ino()));
        assert!(StdUnixStream::connect(&path).is_ok());

        drop(listener);
        drop(guard);
        drop(lock);
        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn refuses_legacy_live_listener_without_sidecar_lock() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-legacy-live-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        let listener = std::os::unix::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let original = fs::symlink_metadata(&path).unwrap();

        let error = bind_core_socket(&path).err().unwrap();
        assert_eq!(error.kind(), io::ErrorKind::AddrInUse);
        assert_eq!(fs::symlink_metadata(&path).unwrap().ino(), original.ino());
        assert!(StdUnixStream::connect(&path).is_ok());

        drop(listener);
        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn never_removes_regular_files_or_symlinks() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-occupied-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        fs::write(&path, "keep me").unwrap();
        assert!(bind_core_socket(&path).is_err());
        assert_eq!(fs::read_to_string(&path).unwrap(), "keep me");

        fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        let target = directory.join("target");
        fs::write(&target, "also keep me").unwrap();
        std::os::unix::fs::symlink(&target, &path).unwrap();
        assert!(bind_core_socket(&path).is_err());
        assert!(
            fs::symlink_metadata(&path)
                .unwrap()
                .file_type()
                .is_symlink()
        );
        assert_eq!(fs::read_to_string(&target).unwrap(), "also keep me");

        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn refuses_recovery_in_world_writable_directory() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-public-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        let stale = std::os::unix::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        drop(stale);
        fs::set_permissions(&directory, fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o777)).unwrap();

        assert!(bind_core_socket(&path).is_err());
        assert!(fs::symlink_metadata(&path).unwrap().file_type().is_socket());

        fs::set_permissions(&directory, fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o700)).unwrap();
        fs::remove_dir_all(directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn guard_removes_owned_socket() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-guard-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        let listener = std::os::unix::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let guard = SocketGuard::new(&path).unwrap();
        drop(listener);
        drop(guard);
        assert!(!path.exists());
        std::fs::remove_dir(&directory).unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn guard_preserves_replacement_socket() {
        let directory = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-core-replacement-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&directory).unwrap();
        let path = directory.join("socket");
        let listener = std::os::unix::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let guard = SocketGuard::new(&path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        let replacement = std::os::unix::net::UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        drop(listener);
        drop(guard);
        assert!(path.exists());
        drop(replacement);
        std::fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(&directory).unwrap();
    }
}

FILE	crates/kira-core/src/niri.rs
//! Niri EventStream plus one deliberately narrow click-to-focus action.
//! Full snapshots and changes are read-only. Only a known workspace ID can
//! be focused; arbitrary actions, windows, outputs and configuration writes
//! are never accepted from the UI. Disconnect clears state and reconnects.

use std::io;
use std::os::unix::fs::FileTypeExt;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
use std::time::Duration;

use kira_ipc::{Workspace, WorkspaceState};
use serde_json::Value;
use tokio::io::{AsyncWriteExt, BufReader};
use tokio::net::UnixStream;
use tokio::sync::watch;

use crate::read_bounded_line;

const MAX_NIRI_LINE: usize = 256 * 1024;
const MAX_WORKSPACES: usize = 256;
const RETRY_DELAY: Duration = Duration::from_secs(1);

pub fn socket_path_from(value: Option<std::ffi::OsString>) -> Option<PathBuf> {
    value.map(PathBuf::from).filter(|path| path.is_absolute())
}

fn invalid(message: &str) -> io::Error {
    io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::InvalidData, message)
}

fn parse_workspaces(value: &Value) -> io::Result<Vec<Workspace>> {
    let list = value
        .as_array()
        .ok_or_else(|| invalid("workspaces not an array"))?;
    if list.len() > MAX_WORKSPACES {
        return Err(invalid("too many workspaces"));
    }
    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(list.len());
    for item in list {
        let id = item["id"]
            .as_u64()
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid("workspace id missing"))?;
        let idx = u8::try_from(
            item["idx"]
                .as_u64()
                .ok_or_else(|| invalid("workspace idx missing"))?,
        )
        .map_err(|_| invalid("invalid workspace idx"))?;
        let name = match item.get("name") {
            None | Some(Value::Null) => None,
            Some(Value::String(text)) => Some(text.clone()),
            _ => return Err(invalid("invalid workspace name")),
        };
        let output = match item.get("output") {
            None | Some(Value::Null) => None,
            Some(Value::String(text)) => Some(text.clone()),
            _ => return Err(invalid("invalid workspace output")),
        };
        result.push(Workspace {
            id: id.to_string(),
            idx,
            name,
            output,
            is_active: item["is_active"]
                .as_bool()
                .ok_or_else(|| invalid("is_active missing"))?,
            is_focused: item["is_focused"]
                .as_bool()
                .ok_or_else(|| invalid("is_focused missing"))?,
            is_urgent: item["is_urgent"]
                .as_bool()
                .ok_or_else(|| invalid("is_urgent missing"))?,
        });
    }
    result.sort_by(|a, b| {
        a.output
            .cmp(&b.output)
            .then(a.idx.cmp(&b.idx))
            .then(a.id.cmp(&b.id))
    });
    Ok(result)
}

/// Apply only the workspace-related variants. Unknown future Niri events are ignored.
/// A malformed supported event is a protocol error and forces a resync.
fn apply_event(state: &mut WorkspaceState, value: &Value) -> io::Result<bool> {
    if let Some(payload) = value.get("WorkspacesChanged") {
        let workspaces = parse_workspaces(&payload["workspaces"])?;
        *state = WorkspaceState {
            connected: true,
            workspaces,
        };
        return Ok(true);
    }
    if !state.connected {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    if let Some(payload) = value.get("WorkspaceActivated") {
        let id = payload["id"]
            .as_u64()
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid("activation id missing"))?
            .to_string();
        let focused = payload["focused"]
            .as_bool()
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid("activation focused missing"))?;
        let Some(target) = state.workspaces.iter().find(|ws| ws.id == id) else {
            // Unknown workspace: wait for the next complete WorkspacesChanged.
            return Ok(false);
        };
        let output = target.output.clone();
        for workspace in &mut state.workspaces {
            if workspace.id == id {
                workspace.is_active = true;
                if focused {
                    workspace.is_focused = true;
                }
            } else {
                if workspace.output == output {
                    workspace.is_active = false;
                }
                if focused {
                    workspace.is_focused = false;
                }
            }
        }
        return Ok(true);
    }
    if let Some(payload) = value.get("WorkspaceUrgencyChanged") {
        let id = payload["id"]
            .as_u64()
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid("urgency id missing"))?
            .to_string();
        let urgent = payload["urgent"]
            .as_bool()
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid("urgency flag missing"))?;
        if let Some(workspace) = state.workspaces.iter_mut().find(|ws| ws.id == id) {
            workspace.is_urgent = urgent;
            return Ok(true);
        }
    }
    Ok(false)
}

async fn run_stream(socket: &Path, sender: &watch::Sender<WorkspaceState>) -> io::Result<()> {
    let stream = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(3), UnixStream::connect(socket))
        .await
        .map_err(|_| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::TimedOut, "niri connect timeout"))??;
    let (reader, mut writer) = stream.into_split();
    writer.write_all(b"\"EventStream\"\n").await?;
    let mut reader = BufReader::new(reader);

    let ack = tokio::time::timeout(
        Duration::from_secs(3),
        read_bounded_line(&mut reader, MAX_NIRI_LINE),
    )
    .await
    .map_err(|_| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::TimedOut, "niri handshake timeout"))??
    .ok_or_else(|| invalid("niri closed before handshake"))?;
    let ack: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&ack)?;
    if ack != serde_json::json!({"Ok": "Handled"}) {
        return Err(invalid("niri rejected EventStream"));
    }
    let mut state = WorkspaceState::default();
    loop {
        let line = read_bounded_line(&mut reader, MAX_NIRI_LINE)
            .await?
            .ok_or_else(|| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::UnexpectedEof, "niri disconnected"))?;
        let event: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&line)?;
        if apply_event(&mut state, &event)? {
            sender.send_replace(state.clone());
        }
    }
}

/// Only accept a stable workspace ID already advertised by the connected
/// compositor. Indexes are per-output and must never be used for clicks.
pub fn validated_focus_id(
    params: Option<&Value>,
    state: &WorkspaceState,
) -> Result<u64, &'static str> {
    let params = params
        .and_then(Value::as_object)
        .ok_or("Expected focus params")?;
    if params.len() != 1 {
        return Err("Only workspace id is allowed");
    }
    let id = params
        .get("id")
        .and_then(Value::as_str)
        .ok_or("Workspace id must be a string")?;
    let parsed = id.parse::<u64>().map_err(|_| "Invalid workspace id")?;
    if parsed.to_string() != id {
        return Err("Non-canonical workspace id");
    }
    if !state.connected {
        return Err("Niri not connected");
    }
    if !state.workspaces.iter().any(|workspace| workspace.id == id) {
        return Err("Unknown workspace id");
    }
    Ok(parsed)
}

/// Sends the *only* supported mutating Niri request, FocusWorkspace by
/// stable u64 ID. Never use a workspace idx or a guessed/default socket.
pub async fn focus_workspace(socket: &Path, workspace_id: u64) -> io::Result<()> {
    let metadata = std::fs::symlink_metadata(socket)?;
    if !metadata.file_type().is_socket() {
        return Err(io::Error::new(
            io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput,
            "Niri socket path is not a socket",
        ));
    }
    let action = serde_json::json!({
        "Action": {"FocusWorkspace": {"reference": {"Id": workspace_id}}}
    });
    tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(3), async {
        let mut stream = UnixStream::connect(socket).await?;
        stream.write_all(action.to_string().as_bytes()).await?;
        stream.write_all(b"\n").await?;
        let mut reader = BufReader::new(stream);
        let line = read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 4096)
            .await?
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid("Niri closed without action response"))?;
        let reply: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&line)?;
        if reply == serde_json::json!({"Ok": "Handled"}) {
            Ok(())
        } else {
            Err(invalid("Niri rejected workspace focus"))
        }
    })
    .await
    .map_err(|_| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::TimedOut, "Niri action timed out"))?
}

/// Monitor the exact supplied NIRI_SOCKET, reconnecting on disconnect.
/// Invalid paths are never substituted with a host/default compositor socket.
pub async fn monitor(socket: PathBuf, sender: watch::Sender<WorkspaceState>) {
    loop {
        if std::fs::metadata(&socket).is_ok_and(|metadata| metadata.file_type().is_socket())
            && let Err(error) = run_stream(&socket, &sender).await
        {
            eprintln!("kira-core: Niri IPC unavailable: {error}");
        }
        // Never keep stale workspace state after an IPC failure.
        sender.send_replace(WorkspaceState::default());
        tokio::time::sleep(RETRY_DELAY).await;
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use serde_json::json;
    use tokio::io::{AsyncBufReadExt, AsyncWriteExt};
    use tokio::net::UnixListener;

    fn ws(id: u64, idx: u8, output: &str, focused: bool) -> Value {
        json!({
            "id": id, "idx": idx, "name": null, "output": output,
            "is_active": focused, "is_focused": focused, "is_urgent": false,
            "active_window_id": null, "future_extra_field": "ignored"
        })
    }

    #[test]
    fn ignores_unknown_fields_and_preserves_multimonitor_id_index() {
        let result =
            parse_workspaces(&json!([ws(90, 2, "HDMI", false), ws(4, 1, "DP", true)])).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(result[0].id, "4");
        assert_eq!(result[1].idx, 2);
        assert_eq!(result[0].output.as_deref(), Some("DP"));
    }

    #[test]
    fn focus_activation_and_urgency_update_without_resetting_other_output() {
        let mut state = WorkspaceState::default();
        apply_event(
            &mut state,
            &json!({"WorkspacesChanged": {
                "workspaces": [ws(1, 1, "DP", true), ws(2, 2, "DP", false), ws(3, 1, "HDMI", false)]
            }}),
        )
        .unwrap();
        assert!(state.connected);
        assert!(
            apply_event(
                &mut state,
                &json!({"WorkspaceActivated": {"id": 2, "focused": true}})
            )
            .unwrap()
        );
        assert!(!state.workspaces[0].is_active);
        assert!(state.workspaces[1].is_active);
        assert!(state.workspaces[1].is_focused);
        assert!(!state.workspaces[2].is_focused);
        assert!(
            apply_event(
                &mut state,
                &json!({"WorkspaceUrgencyChanged": {"id": 3, "urgent": true}})
            )
            .unwrap()
        );
        assert!(state.workspaces[2].is_urgent);
        assert!(
            apply_event(
                &mut state,
                &json!({"WorkspaceActivated": {"id": 3, "focused": false}})
            )
            .unwrap()
        );
        assert!(state.workspaces[1].is_focused); // activation without focus does not change global focus
    }

    #[test]
    fn rejects_malformed_workspace_payload_without_fake_connected_state() {
        let mut state = WorkspaceState::default();
        assert!(
            apply_event(
                &mut state,
                &json!({"WorkspacesChanged": {"workspaces": [{"id": 1}]}})
            )
            .is_err()
        );
        assert!(!state.connected);
        assert!(socket_path_from(Some("relative.sock".into())).is_none());
        assert!(socket_path_from(None).is_none());
    }

    #[test]
    fn focus_rejects_offline_unknown_noncanonical_and_non_string_ids() {
        let state = WorkspaceState {
            connected: true,
            workspaces: vec![Workspace {
                id: u64::MAX.to_string(),
                idx: 2,
                name: None,
                output: Some("DP".into()),
                is_active: false,
                is_focused: false,
                is_urgent: false,
            }],
        };
        assert_eq!(
            validated_focus_id(Some(&json!({"id": u64::MAX.to_string()})), &state),
            Ok(u64::MAX)
        );
        for invalid in [
            json!({"id":2}),
            json!({"id":"02"}),
            json!({"idx":2}),
            json!({"id":"2"}),
            json!({"id":"-1"}),
            json!({"id":"18446744073709551616"}),
            json!({"id": u64::MAX.to_string(), "action":"quit"}),
        ] {
            assert!(
                validated_focus_id(Some(&invalid), &state).is_err(),
                "{invalid}"
            );
        }
        assert!(validated_focus_id(None, &state).is_err());
        assert!(
            validated_focus_id(
                Some(&json!({"id":u64::MAX.to_string()})),
                &WorkspaceState::default()
            )
            .is_err()
        );
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn focus_action_targets_exact_workspace_id_and_handles_niri_error() {
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("kira-focus-{}", std::process::id()));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        let path = dir.join("niri.sock");
        let listener = UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let server = tokio::spawn(async move {
            for ok in [true, false] {
                let (socket, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
                let (reader, mut writer) = socket.into_split();
                let mut reader = BufReader::new(reader);
                let line = read_bounded_line(&mut reader, 4096).await.unwrap().unwrap();
                let request: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&line).unwrap();
                assert_eq!(
                    request,
                    json!({"Action":{"FocusWorkspace":{"reference":{"Id":u64::MAX}}}})
                );
                writer
                    .write_all(if ok {
                        b"{\"Ok\":\"Handled\"}\n"
                    } else {
                        b"{\"Err\":\"No such workspace\"}\n"
                    })
                    .await
                    .unwrap();
            }
        });
        assert!(focus_workspace(&path, u64::MAX).await.is_ok());
        assert!(focus_workspace(&path, u64::MAX).await.is_err());
        server.await.unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_file(path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(dir).unwrap();
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn mocked_socket_sends_only_event_stream_and_applies_updates() {
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(
            "kira-niri-test-{}-{:?}",
            std::process::id(),
            std::thread::current().id()
        ));
        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();
        let path = dir.join("niri.sock");
        let listener = UnixListener::bind(&path).unwrap();
        let task = tokio::spawn(async move {
            let (stream, _) = listener.accept().await.unwrap();
            let (reader, mut writer) = stream.into_split();
            let mut reader = BufReader::new(reader);
            let mut request = String::new();
            reader.read_line(&mut request).await.unwrap();
            assert_eq!(request, "\"EventStream\"\n");
            writer.write_all(b"{\"Ok\":\"Handled\"}\n").await.unwrap();
            writer
                .write_all(
                    (json!({"WorkspacesChanged": {"workspaces": [ws(70, 1, "winit", true)]}})
                        .to_string()
                        + "\n")
                        .as_bytes(),
                )
                .await
                .unwrap();
            tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(40)).await;
            writer
                .write_all(b"{\"WorkspaceUrgencyChanged\":{\"id\":70,\"urgent\":true}}\n")
                .await
                .unwrap();
        });
        let (tx, mut rx) = watch::channel(WorkspaceState::default());
        let result = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2), run_stream(&path, &tx))
            .await
            .unwrap();
        assert!(result.is_err()); // mock closed its IPC socket
        rx.changed().await.unwrap();
        let last = rx.borrow().clone();
        assert!(last.connected);
        assert_eq!(last.workspaces[0].output.as_deref(), Some("winit"));
        assert!(last.workspaces[0].is_urgent);
        task.await.unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_file(&path).unwrap();
        std::fs::remove_dir(&dir).unwrap();
    }
}

