# UI architecture: Rust host, Svelte 5 widgets

The architecture contract in [SPECIFICATION.md](SPECIFICATION.md) is explicit:
**all built-in and third-party widgets are authored in Svelte 5**. GTK4,
gtk4-layer-shell and WebKitGTK provide native Wayland surfaces and a trusted
bridge, not a second UI component framework.

## Ownership

| Layer | Responsibility | Must not own |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kira Core (Rust) | Validated configuration, Niri integration, daemon IPC | Rendering widgets |
| Kira Shell (Rust/GTK/WebKit) | Layer-shell windows, focus, lifecycle, permissions; GIO and system-data adapters | Calendars, search lists, layouts or process tables built from GTK widgets |
| Svelte 5 / Tailwind | Top Bar, launcher, calendar, system monitor, processes, future user widgets | Raw shell commands, unvalidated Niri/OS privileges |
| Typed WebKit bridge | Minimal allowlisted native calls; read-only events | Generic command execution or navigation to outside content |

The top bar's 42 px exclusive zone **cannot contain popovers**. The Calendar, System Monitor and Launcher share **one** non-exclusive GTK
layer-shell window and prewarmed WebKit view. At most one Svelte widget is
mounted at a time; the rest own no live timers or DOM. The Launcher
clears all Wayland layer-shell anchors and uses exclusive zone -1 so the
compositor centers it on the full output. Calendar and System Monitor
restore the top/right anchors, 25px top margin, 12px right margin and
exclusive zone 0 when selected. The same GTK window and WebKit view
survive these repositionings. **When switching between the centered
Launcher and corner popups, the GTK surface is first unmapped**, its
anchors are changed while hidden, and remapping is deferred one compositor
turn; the previous WebKit framebuffer must never travel visibly across
the output. Calendar ↔ System remain immediate, in-place switches. The
browser cannot create an ordinary
top-level window with the required layer-shell Wayland behavior by itself.

## Migration, in small reviewable steps

1. **Calendar Svelte implementation and host integration (this PR).**
   The active Calendar is `CalendarWidget.svelte`, mounted inside an
   independent non-exclusive GTK layer-shell window with WebKit. The
   same self-contained HTML bundle is marked with
   `data-kira-surface="calendar"` before `load_html()`; only the
   fixed-purpose `kiraCalendarUi` handler (close, validated ISO date copy)
   is registered there. The Top Bar retains its original 42px reservation.
   The GTK date-grid view and its native CSS have been removed.
2. **Calendar graphic acceptance.** Frontend, GTK/Nix, and security contract
   tests run in CI. The actual separate Wayland window still needs a
   manual nested-Niri graphical smoke-test at multiple scales before release.
3. **Launcher (implemented).** Svelte owns search, selection, layout and
   keyboard events. Rust GIO discovers desktop entries and launches by
   bounded, generation-scoped catalog index. Browser cannot supply executable
   paths or shell commands. Application icons are resolved on demand through GTK IconTheme and delivered
   as bounded image data URIs; missing icons retain the letter fallback.
4. **System Monitor / processes (implemented).** The existing warm WebKit
   overlay now mounts `SystemWidget.svelte` or `CalendarWidget.svelte` on
   demand, never both. Rust keeps read-only kernel metrics, a bounded
   /proc sampler and clipboard report generation. Processes are sampled
   only while their tab is active; Svelte owns the search/sort/table.
5. Remove GTK-only presentation assets, duplicate native color tokens and
   unused view models *only after* the Svelte replacements are functioning.
   Update docs and enforce widget ownership in regression tests.

## Acceptance before releasing the migrated calendar

- NixOS CI: native Shell, frontend type-check, model tests and full package.
- Nested Niri: popup stays inside 360x640 and 600x480 logical displays,
  remains dismissible, and does not enlarge the 42 px Top Bar.
- Keyboard: focus visible on selected Orange day, Tab, Enter, Escape,
  navigation and copy. Pointer: day selection, adjacent months, Today.
- UI events can only reach explicitly allowlisted Rust host operations.
- No duplicate native GTK calendar stays in the shipping Shell.

The calendar is connected in the Shell now. A green CI validates compilation
and contracts, **not** final visual behavior under a real Wayland compositor.
Nested Niri graphical QA remains mandatory before release.

## Lazy widget lifetime and memory ownership

The Calendar layer-shell popup prewarms its **WebKit host** when the bar starts,
but does not mount a Svelte widget until the user opens it. The trusted GTK
host dispatches `kira:calendar:show` with a generation ID, then waits for
`mounted:<generation>` and a double animation frame before revealing the
window. On hide it dispatches `kira:calendar:hide`; the Svelte lifecycle
serially awaits `unmount()`, releasing Calendar DOM, effects, window listeners
and its one-second clock interval. Stale asynchronous mounts/frames are ignored.

The widget is **lazy-instantiated**; its component code is already present
in the single offline HTML bundle, but the DOM, effects, timers and component
instance are created only on show. The live instance is unloaded on hide.
This does **not** unload the prebundled JS bytes or the base WebKit engine. WebKit stays warm for near-instant reopening. RSS/PSS may not
immediately fall because the JavaScript engine retains allocated pages and
shared libraries. All three built-in overlays (Calendar, System Monitor,
Launcher) share the same WebView; the launcher exclusively requests keyboard
focus while active. The GTK widget view and native CSS have been retired.


### Content-sized popup geometry

Calendar, System Monitor and Launcher use **natural Svelte content height** rather
than the old 620px fixed GTK window size. `observeOverlaySize` reads the
active widget's root `getBoundingClientRect().height` and sends
`size:<generation>:<height>` through the private, allowlisted WebKit bridge.
Rust rejects stale generations and invalid sizes and clamps GTK's default
height to **70% of the current output's logical height**. The native output
height is passed to Svelte as an absolute CSS-pixel `maxHeight`: never use
`70vh` here, because WebKit viewport height is itself controlled by GTK and
can form a layout feedback loop. Under the cap the window hugs its content;
over it, Calendar/Overview scroll vertically, while Launcher/Processes scroll
their result lists. `ResizeObserver` is disconnected when Svelte unmounts,
and the original single warm WebView and safe center/corner relocation remain.

FILE	docs/VISUAL_REVIEW.md
# Kira Desktop — visual design review

**Reviewed:** 2026-11-01  
**Branch:** `feat/neo-editorial-shell` · PR #18  
**Reference:** [DESIGN_SYSTEM.md](DESIGN_SYSTEM.md), [SPECIFICATION.md §15](SPECIFICATION.md#15-премиальный-ui-и-фирменная-палитра-обязательное-требование), and user-provided nested-Niri screenshots.

## Scope and verdict

Reviewed the **currently implemented** Svelte Top Bar, GTK Launcher,
custom GTK Calendar, canonical color tokens, typography, hover/focus/selected/
disabled/error states, popup geometry, and visual QA. Dock, notifications,
settings surfaces, and configurable themes **do not yet exist** and therefore
cannot be signed off.

**Design direction: GOOD. Visual acceptance: CONDITIONAL.** The Black /
Prussian Blue / Orange / Alabaster Grey / White palette is preserved. The
Top Bar uses three functional color zones and a compact system group; Launcher
and Calendar use Black editorial headings, Blue working regions and restrained
local Orange states. Double-bordered cards and offset widget shadows are
absent from the implemented UI. The most recent user screenshots show
substantially improved compositional coherence.

This audit is based on repository source and screenshots already supplied
in the conversation. **No new pixel-by-pixel rendering or visual run in Niri
was performed by the reviewer.** Build, type-check and source-string tests
cannot substitute for actual display-scale and interaction acceptance.

## Verified deviations fixed as part of this review

| Priority | Issue and evidence | Correction |
| --- | --- | --- |
| P1 | [Calendar day selection](../crates/kira-shell/src/calendar.css): selected day is Orange, but the generic focus outline is also Orange. Contrast of the focus edge against its selected fill is **1:1**. | Add an inset **Black** outline specifically for `.kira-day-selected:focus-visible`. Contrast Black/Orange is approximately **10.39:1**. |
| P1 | [Calendar adjacent-month days](../crates/kira-shell/src/calendar.css) used `rgba(229,229,229,0.5)` over Prussian Blue, approximately **4.20:1**, despite being interactive 12px text. Specification requires normal text >= 4.5:1. | Increase opacity to **0.60** (approximately **5.44:1**); add a numeric contrast regression test. |
| P1 | [Workspace focus](../frontend/src/lib/components/WorkspacePreview.svelte) used a White outline for a selected Orange chip: White/Orange is only **2.02:1**, and the positive offset places focus against dark surrounding material. | Change selected-state focus to an **inset Black** outline on Orange. Ordinary workspace focus remains Orange. |

The fixes above are source-backed changes, not claimed visually verified
until a screenshot/keyboard test is performed in Niri.

## Outstanding findings

| Priority | Surface | Finding | Required acceptance |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **P1** | Calendar, Launcher | [Calendar](../crates/kira-shell/src/calendar.rs) uses a fixed **378×490** default size, Top margin **50**, Right **12**. [Launcher](../crates/kira-shell/src/launcher.rs) uses **600×520**, Top margin **58**. No monitor-aware clamping or adaptive layout is visible. **Potential** clipping on narrow/short outputs or large text; not proven in the provided screenshots. | Test logical displays **360×640, 600×480, 800×600**, window scaling 100/125/150/200%; add bounds-aware position and scroll/collapse if failure reproduced. Ensure that close/Today/Copy remain reachable. |
| **P1** | Visual QA | [qa_visual.py](../scripts/qa_visual.py) optionally captures nested Niri at four scales but does **not** open Launcher/Calendar, exercise interaction states, or judge screenshots automatically. Existing static CSS tests verify selector presence, not pixels. | Expand explicit opt-in screenshot matrix to include both open overlays, selected and focused controls, and warning states; review images manually and save acceptance notes. No automatic false-green “visual pass”. |
| **P2** | Top Bar | [App.svelte](../frontend/src/App.svelte) uses a **42px** `overflow-hidden` root and several `shrink-0` warnings/right-hand controls. With many workspace names and error messages, a narrow viewport may clip useful content. Current tests look for class strings rather than overflow outcomes. | Test 360, 540, 800, 1024 and 1280 logical widths with **1/8/32 workspaces**, long localized names, seconds enabled and Core/Niri/calendar error labels. Preserve clock and keyboard access; degrade secondary metadata first. |
| **P2** | Typography | Top Bar overline is **8px**; secondary labels in GTK calendar/Launcher are often **10px**, date help **10px**, descriptions **11px**. Size alone is not a WCAG violation, but can undermine the promised readable “premium” hierarchy. | Review readability at 100/125/150/200% and varying font settings; target at least **10–11px for functional metadata** where layout allows. Large editorial headings can remain distinctive. |
| **P2** | Typographic identity | The Svelte theme declares an Inter/Segoe/Noto stack while both native GTK styles rely on the environment's GTK font. Cyrillic date labels are locale-rendered, but controls read `TODAY`, `COPY DATE`, `APPLICATION CATALOG`, etc. This may feel inconsistent when moving between three surfaces. | Specify a shared **typographic hierarchy** and Cyrillic-capable fallback on GTK; decide whether interface copy is intentionally English or localized. Verify month-name widths and fallback glyphs. |
| **P2** | Calendar controls | [Calendar CSS](../crates/kira-shell/src/calendar.css) includes the proper keyboard-focus selectors, but `Today`, `Copy Date`, arrow groups, selected and current days still require real pointer+keyboard state review. An HTML `aria-haspopup="dialog"` exists on the clock, but no `aria-expanded` state is tracked across the separate GTK window. | Tab/Shift+Tab, Enter, arrow navigation, ESC, PageUp/Down, Home, copying, and opening/closing by pointer and keyboard; ensure consistently visible focus and expected accessible state across process boundaries. |
| **P3** | Token/code hygiene | [kira-default.css](../frontend/src/lib/themes/kira-default.css) retains unused `--kira-border-strong`, `--kira-shadow-brutal` and `--kira-shadow-panel`. These legacy concepts contradict the restrained, near-borderless current style if reused indiscriminately. Canonical color values are also repeated in GTK CSS. | Deprecate/remove dead tokens after downstream search; keep cross-surface canonical palette and style tests, not manual divergence. |
| **P3** | Documentation | Specification §15 previously called Launcher and Calendar future work; the implementation now contains both. | Update status accurately (done in this audit); maintain explicit *implemented vs visually accepted* distinction. |

## Design-system conformity matrix

| Principle | Finding | Evidence / limits |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Five canonical colors | **Pass** | Typed palette + Svelte token aliases + named GTK color declarations match five agreed values. Derived rgba and color-mixes are allowed. |
| Neo-Brutalist geometry | **Pass** | Single strong selected workspace, orange active rail in Launcher, own date picker with restrained states. No return of stacked borders and hard offset widget shadows. |
| Editorial hierarchy | **Pass with caveats** | Clear hero/working/footer zones and strong scale contrast. Microcopy sizes and cross-framework font parity still need verification. |
| Expressive minimalism | **Pass** | Few accent fills, informationally useful surfaces, flat Today/Copy text actions. |
| Keyboard and contrast | **Fixed deviations, pending acceptance** | Focus and adjacent-day contrast fixes in code. Actual GTK keyboard-focus visuals still unconfirmed. |
| Responsive geometry | **Unverified / at risk** | Responsive Top Bar classes exist; GTK windows have fixed default dimensions. |
| Visual regression evidence | **Not accepted** | CI is valuable for compilation and behavior, but no reviewed screenshots for the current branch at all required sizes/states. |

## Recommended next acceptance pass

1. **Block on accessibility:** build and inspect the new inset Black focus ring on both Calendar's selected Orange day and focused Orange workspace; confirm adjacent-month days are readable.
2. **Block on clipping:** check 360×640, 600×480, 800×600 and 1024×768 logical sizes, then 100/125/150/200% scales. Popovers must stay visible and be dismissible.
3. **Verify status/error variants:** Niri disconnected, Core disconnected/connecting, long workspace names, multiple workspaces, clock seconds and local date.
4. **Verify native controls:** Launcher search/row selection/scroll/Enter/Esc; Calendar Today/Copy/month-year navigation/adjacent months, tooltips and Tab focus.
5. **Only then approve visual identity** and update [QA_VISUAL.md](QA_VISUAL.md) with actual inspected screenshots and results. Do not merge a “visual-ready” claim based only on CI.

**Verdict:** architecture and brand language meet the intent; the remaining
scope is measured polish and verified responsive/accessibility behavior, not
another aesthetic redesign.

## KISS / DRY follow-up: native overlay infrastructure

The Launcher and Calendar previously each declared all five identical
`@define-color` values and repeated GTK CSS-provider installation and window
lookup/dismiss logic. Shared canonical GTK declarations now live in
`native-palette.css` and the small `native_ui.rs` helper. This deliberately
**does not** unify their layouts or behavior: these surfaces have different
interaction models. Nix explicitly retains the new stylesheet, and one
cross-surface test checks canonical palette alignment and assembly.

FILE	flake.nix
{
  description = "Kira Desktop: NixOS-first Wayland shell built on Niri";

  inputs.nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
  # Pinned Crane release; Cargo dependencies compile in a separate derivation.
  inputs.crane.url = "github:ipetkov/crane/eb35abda9f232cc6610b1d1e3200d15c49b7ac54";

  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, crane }:
    let
      systems = [ "x86_64-linux" "aarch64-linux" ];
      forAllSystems = f:
        nixpkgs.lib.genAttrs systems (system: f nixpkgs.legacyPackages.${system});

      # Expose the package when the application sources and locks exist.
      hasApplicationSources =
        builtins.pathExists ./Cargo.toml
        && builtins.pathExists ./Cargo.lock
        && builtins.pathExists ./frontend/package.json
        && builtins.pathExists ./frontend/package-lock.json;
    in
    {
      devShells = forAllSystems (pkgs: {
        default = pkgs.mkShell {
          packages = with pkgs; [
            cargo
            rustc
            sccache # persistent compiler cache for local cargo builds
            rustfmt
            clippy
            nodejs
            go-task
            python3
            niri
            foot # optional nested Niri terminal for interactive workspace QA
            grim # explicit visual QA screenshot capture, does not copy clipboard
            pkg-config
            gtk4
            gtk4-layer-shell
            webkitgtk_6_0
            pipewire
          ];
          # Local Cargo uses a persistent compiler cache; sandboxed nix build
          # instead reuses Crane's immutable Rust dependency derivation.
          shellHook = ''
            export RUSTC_WRAPPER="${pkgs.sccache}/bin/sccache"
            export SCCACHE_DIR="''${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/kira-desktop/sccache"
            export SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE="''${SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE:-10G}"
          '';
        };
        # Native Shell type-checking in PRs: no compositor, JS toolchain,
        # screenshot tools or interactive terminal needed. This shell uses
        # cache.nixos.org (and optional Cachix in CI) for GTK/WebKit inputs;
        # Rust artifacts are cached separately by GitHub Actions.
        ci = pkgs.mkShell {
          packages = with pkgs; [
            cargo
            rustc
            pkg-config
            gtk4
            gtk4-layer-shell
            webkitgtk_6_0
            pipewire
          ];
        };
      });

      packages = forAllSystems (pkgs:
        if hasApplicationSources
        then
          let
            app = pkgs.callPackage ./nix/package.nix { craneLib = crane.mkLib pkgs; };
          in {
            default = app;
            # Fast isolated UI build, useful for validating npmDepsHash without
            # compiling GTK/WebKit Rust dependencies.
            frontend = app.frontend;
          }
        else { }
      );

      checks = forAllSystems (pkgs: {
        repository-spec = pkgs.runCommand "kira-desktop-spec-check" { } ''
          test -s ${./docs/SPECIFICATION.md}
          test -s ${./nix/package.nix}
          test -s ${./Taskfile.yml}
          test -s ${./.github/workflows/ci.yml}
          touch "$out"
        '';
      });
    };
}

FILE	frontend/index.html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000ff" />
    <title>Kira Desktop</title>
    <script>
      // Head runs before the compiled Svelte bundle. Track boot milestones
      // so failures are distinguishable from resource/scheme errors.
      window.__kiraBoot = { head: true, lastError: null };
      const report = (message) => {
        try {
          window.webkit?.messageHandlers?.kiraDiagnostics?.postMessage(message);
        } catch (error) {
          // Diagnostics must never prevent the Svelte entrypoint from loading.
          console.warn('Kira diagnostics bridge unavailable:', error);
        }
      };
      report('HTML head script executed; location=' + location.href);

      window.addEventListener('error', (event) => {
        const error = event.error;
        const details = [
          'error: ' + String(event.message || error?.message || 'unknown'),
          'source=' + String(event.filename || location.href),
          'line=' + String(event.lineno || 0),
          'column=' + String(event.colno || 0),
          error?.stack ? 'stack=' + String(error.stack) : '',
        ].filter(Boolean).join(' | ');
        window.__kiraBoot.lastError = details;
        report(details);
      });
      window.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (event) => {
        const reason = event.reason;
        const details = 'unhandled rejection: ' + String(reason?.stack || reason);
        window.__kiraBoot.lastError = details;
        report(details);
      });
      window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          const pending = document.querySelector('#kira-loading');
          if (pending) {
            const stage = JSON.stringify({
              ...window.__kiraBoot,
              entryStarted: window.__kiraEntryStarted === true,
              mountReturned: window.__kiraMountReturned === true,
            });
            pending.textContent = window.__kiraBoot.bootstrapError
              ? 'Kira UI error: ' + String(window.__kiraBoot.bootstrapError).slice(0,220)
              : 'Kira UI did not start (' + stage + '). Check terminal logs.';
            report('Svelte not mounted: ' + stage);
          }
        }, 2500);
      });
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="app">
      <div id="kira-loading" style="height:42px; display:flex; align-items:center; padding:0 14px; font:12px system-ui; background:#000000ff; color:#ffffffff;">
        Kira Desktop · Loading interface…
      </div>
    </div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>

